          "heading": "Darcy Graham sidelined until next year as Josh McKay nears Scotland call",
          "body": "Edinburgh wing Darcy Graham will remain unavailable until the end of the year after suffering a ruptured bicep. Head coach Sean Everitt described the injury as freakish, with the blow ruling the finisher out of the November test series. Consequently, Glasgow Warriors full-back Josh McKay is being tipped for a potential debut. McKay has been a consistent performer since 2021 and is now eligible to provide depth behind Blair Kinghorn and Kyle Rowe in the Nations Championship."
